{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260523183806211b811edd9f473e","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.1","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of both games. Let me now create tasks and run the full test suite. Let me also check for any remaining files and the existing test file for match3.\n\nKey observations so far:\n\n**Match3 Game:**\n1. Touch events - InputHandler.js handles both mouse and touch events with `passive: false` and `preventDefault()` ✓\n2. Canvas resize - Renderer.resize() handles DPR, window.innerWidth/Height ✓\n3. Navigation touch - index.html has touchend handler for nav screens ✓\n4. The `active` flag on InputHandler properly skips touch interception when nav screens are showing ✓\n5. Back-to-map button has both click and touchend handlers ✓\n\n**Idiom Game:**\n1. Uses DOM rendering (HTML elements) - no Canvas ✓\n2. CSS has `touch-action: manipulation` ✓\n3. Buttons use `onclick` which works on both click and touch ✓\n4. `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch` on scrollable areas ✓\n5. Uses `alert()` for error messages - potential issue in Douyin runtime ✓\n6. Text input has proper mobile attributes (`autocomplete=\"off\"`, `enterkeyhint=\"search\"`) ✓\n\nLet me check for existing test files and read more files to complete the analysis.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7463fb62-2e03-4edd-abad-466ff792dff1","uuid":"e78baf4d-2970-4d23-b55c-9b99db77da4a"}
